'.source.gfm, .text.md':
  '{number}{element}':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-inline'
    'body': '{${1:number}}{${2:__element__}}'
    'description': """
      Use simple inline effects to highlight specific elements within a Markdown block. Simply enclose your elements within two subsequent braces ({}{}), whereby the first one is used to hold the number of appearance, while the will contain your text, image, video, what so ever ...
      You can tweak your effects with additional animations and styling. Animate.css is included at default.

      Examples:
        This block contains some {1}{inline __effects__} that will appear {2}{subsequently}.

        Inline effects can also contain more effects {1}{I will appear first {2}{and I as a second}}.

        With styling ++ {3}{bouncing red and delayed}<!--
              class = "animated infinite bounce"
              style = "animation-delay: 3s; color: red;"
            -->
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'


  '{from-to}{element}':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-inline2'
    'body': '{${1:from}-${2:to}}{${3:__element__}}'
    'description': """
      Use simple inline effects to highlight specific elements within a Markdown block. Simply enclose your elements within two subsequent braces ({}{}), whereby the first one contains two numbers separated by (-) the first number defines the time of appearance and the second one the time of disappearance. The element contains the Markdown elements for highlighting (text, videos, images, etc.)
      You can tweak your effects with additional animations and styling. Animate.css is included at default.

      Examples:
        This block contains some {1-2}{I appear at fragment 1 and disapper at 2}.

        Nesting is allowed but has to make sense {1-3}{I will rest from 1 to 3 {4}{I will not be visible}}.

        With styling ++ {1-3}{bouncing red and delayed}<!--
              class = "animated infinite bounce"
              style = "animation-delay: 3s; color: red;"
            -->
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'

  '{{number}}':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-block'
    'body': '    {{${1:number}}}\n$2'
    'body2': '    {{number}}'
    'description': """
      Use block effects to let an entire Markdown block appear at a certain animation step. Put the step number in double braces on its own line directly above the block. Indent it by 4 or more spaces, so that other Markdown viewers show it as code and not as text. In Textbook mode all blocks are visible and tagged with their step number.
      The entire block can also be styled and the animation tweaked, but the required comment tag has to be defined before the Markdown block. Animate.css is included at default.

      Examples:
                          {{1}}
        This entire block will appear with the first
        fragment. And remain till the end of this slide.

                          {{2}}
        ```js
        // this works with any markdown block
        ```

        <!-- class = "animated rollIn" -->
             {{3}}
        | Also | with  |
        |------|-------|
        | any  | table |
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'


  '{{from-to}}':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-block2'
    'body': '    {{${1:from}-${2:to}}}\n$3'
    'body2': '    {{from-to}}'
    'description': """
      Use block effects with a range to let an entire Markdown block appear at the first step and disappear at the second. Put both numbers, separated by a hyphen, in double braces directly above the block.
      The entire block can also be styled and the animation tweaked, but the required comment tag has to be defined before the Markdown block. Animate.css is included at default.

      Examples:
                         {{1-4}}
        This entire block will appear with the first fragment.
        And remain until the fourth fragment of this slide.

                         {{0-1}}
        ```js
        // I will be present immediately and disappear on the
        // 1st fragment.
        ```

        <!-- class = "animated rollIn" -->
             {{3-4}}
        | Also | with  |
        |------|-------|
        | any  | table |
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'


  '{{number}} *** ... ***':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-multiblock'
    'body': """
                       {{${1:number}}}
      ************************************************

      ${2:Insert your Markdown blocks in here ...}

      ************************************************
    """
    'description': """
      Bundle multiple blocks into one animation step by enclosing them in two lines of three or more asterisks (*). The effect definition goes above the opening line. Alternatively, use a <section> ... </section> wrapper instead of the asterisks (see lia-effect-section).
      The entire block can also be styled and the animation tweaked, but the required comment tag has to be defined before the Markdown block. Animate.css is included at default.

      Examples:
                          {{1}}
        *************************************************

        Both blocks will appear at once. Nesting of other
        {2}{inline} and block effects is also allowed.


        | Also | with  |
        |------|-------|
        | any  | table |

        **************************************************
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'


  '{{from-to}} *** ... ***':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-multiblock2'
    'body': """
                       {{${1:from}-${2:to}}}
      ************************************************

      ${3:Insert your Markdown blocks in here ...}

      ************************************************
    """
    'description': """
      Bundle multiple blocks into one animation step by enclosing them in two lines of three or more asterisks (*). The effect definition goes above the opening line. Alternatively, use a <section> ... </section> wrapper instead of the asterisks (see lia-effect-section).
      The entire block can also be styled and the animation tweaked, but the required comment tag has to be defined before the Markdown block. Animate.css is included at default.

      Examples:
                          {{1-3}}
        *************************************************

        Both blocks will appear at once and disappear at
        the third fragment. Nesting of other {2}{inline}
        and block effects is also allowed.


        | Also | with  |
        |------|-------|
        | any  | table |

        **************************************************
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'

  '<!-- class="animated rollIn" ... -->':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-animate-example'
    'body': '<!-- class="animated rollIn" style="animation-delay: 3s;" -->'
    'description': """
      This is only an example of how Animate.css can be used to tweak your effects. Additional CSS magic can be applied onto single elements or blocks by adding a comment tag either in front of the block or directly after the element.

      Example:

        <!-- class = "animated rollIn" style = "animation-delay: 3s; color: purple" -->
        The whole text-block should appear in purple color and with a wobbling effect.
        Which is a **bad** example, please use it with caution ...
        ~~ Jumping red ~~ <!-- class = "animated infinite bounce" style = "color: red;" -->

      For more information how to change the animation styles, click on the link below.
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://animate.style'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'


  '{|>}{read this text}':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-inline-playback'
    'body': '{|>}{${1:text to read}}'
    'description': """
      With this triangle notation it is possible to add a playback button, which will read out loud the text within the second braces. It is possible to add additional animation definitions and also to change the voice.

      Start typing voice, if you want to change the narrator and the language.

      Examples:
        Within this block {|>}{this text will be spoken out loud}.

        Nesting is allowed but has to make sense {1-3 |>}{I speak from 1 to 3 {4}{and nesting is also possible}}.

        If you want to {|> Australian Female}{it is also possible to change the voice}.
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'

  '{{|>}}':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-block-playback'
    'body': '{{|>}}'
    'description': """
      Use the `|>` or `!>` to indicate, that the entire block below should be read out loud in the default language. It is also possible to add effect-numbers to indicate the appearance and also to add another language. Start typing "voice" to select another narrator and language.

      Example:

           {{|>}}
        Read this block after the user has clicked the play button.

           {{3 |>}}
        This block will only appear at the 3rd animation step.

           {{1-2 |> Australian Female}}
        This will appear at step 1 and disappear at animation step 2, when the
        users clicks on it, an Australian female voice is used as a narrator.
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'

  '{{|> voice}}':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-block-playback-voice'
    'body': '    {{|> ${1:voice}}}\n$2'
    'body_vscode': '    {{|> ${1|UK English Female,UK English Male,US English Female,US English Male,Afrikaans Male,Albanian Male,Arabic Female,Arabic Male,Armenian Male,Australian Female,Australian Male,Bangla Bangladesh Female,Bangla Bangladesh Male,Bangla India Female,Bangla India Male,Bosnian Male,Brazilian Portuguese Female,Brazilian Portuguese Male,Catalan Male,Chinese Female,Chinese Male,Chinese (Hong Kong) Female,Chinese (Hong Kong) Male,Chinese Taiwan Female,Chinese Taiwan Male,Croatian Male,Czech Female,Czech Male,Danish Female,Danish Male,Deutsch Female,Deutsch Male,Dutch Female,Dutch Male,Esperanto Male,Estonian Male,Filipino Female,Finnish Female,Finnish Male,French Canadian Female,French Canadian Male,French Female,French Male,Greek Female,Greek Male,Hindi Female,Hindi Male,Hungarian Female,Hungarian Male,Icelandic Male,Indonesian Female,Indonesian Male,Italian Female,Italian Male,Japanese Female,Japanese Male,Korean Female,Korean Male,Latin Female,Latin Male,Latvian Male,Macedonian Male,Moldavian Female,Moldavian Male,Montenegrin Male,Nepali,Nepali,Norwegian Female,Norwegian Male,Polish Female,Polish Male,Portuguese Female,Portuguese Male,Romanian Female,Romanian Male,Russian Female,Russian Male,Serbian Male,Serbo-Croatian Male,Sinhala,Sinhala,Slovak Female,Slovak Male,Spanish Female,Spanish Male,Spanish Latin American Female,Spanish Latin American Male,Swahili Male,Swedish Female,Swedish Male,Tamil Female,Tamil Male,Thai Female,Thai Male,Turkish Female,Turkish Male,Ukrainian Female,Vietnamese Female,Vietnamese Male,Welsh Male|}}}\n$2'
    'description': """
      Adds a play button to the block below, which reads it out loud with the given voice instead of the default narrator. The button works in every mode and does not depend on the animation steps.

      Type "voice" to search all available voices.

      Example:
            {{|> Australian Female}}
        This paragraph is read with an Australian voice.

            {{1 |> Deutsch Female}}
        Dieser Absatz erscheint bei Schritt 1 und wird auf Deutsch vorgelesen.
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'


  '{{number}} <section> ... </section>':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-section'
    'body': """
                       {{${1:number}}}
      <section>

      ${2:Insert your Markdown blocks in here ...}

      </section>
    """
    'description': """
      Groups multiple blocks into one animation step with an HTML section tag instead of two lines of asterisks. Leave a blank line after <section> and before </section>, so that the content is parsed as Markdown.

      Example:
                          {{1}}
        <section>

        This paragraph and the table below appear together.

        | Also | with  |
        |------|-------|
        | any  | table |

        </section>
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'


  'presentation slide: {{n}} + --{{n}}--':
    'prefix': 'lia-effect-presentation'
    'body': """
      ## ${1:Slide Title}

                   --{{0}}--
      ${2:Introduction, spoken when the slide is opened.}

                     {{1}}
      ${3:* First bullet point}

                   --{{1}}--
      ${4:Narration for the first bullet point.}

                     {{2}}
      ${5:* Second bullet point}

                   --{{2}}--
      ${6:Narration for the second bullet point.}
    """
    'description': """
      A slide that works as a presentation and as a textbook: every visible step {{n}} is paired with a narration --{{n}}-- for the same step. Think of {{n}} as the bullet point and --{{n}}-- as the speaker notes for it.

      How the narration is shown depends on the mode:
        Presentation -> spoken, text hidden
        Slides       -> spoken, text shown in the side panel
        Textbook     -> not spoken, text shown in place

      A --{{n}}-- comment alone never reveals anything on the slide, so always pair it with a {{n}} block. Step 0 introduces the slide.

      Example:
        ## Photosynthesis

                     --{{0}}--
        Plants turn light into sugar. Let us look at the inputs.

                       {{1}}
        * Light, water and CO2 go in

                     --{{1}}--
        Three things are needed: light, water and carbon dioxide.
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">💫</span>'

